   <media:description>In 1900, Professor Isabel Bevier came to campus with bold ideas. By 1920, her leadership transformed the recognition of women in academia. As head of the Department of Household Sciences at the University of Illinois, she championed the application of scientific knowledge to improve everyday life. More than a century later, her legacy continues to shape our campus community.

To learn more, visit: 
https://beviercafe.illinois.edu/</media:description>
